Quizzle (for TAC-368)

Write a Flutter program that reads a file of question-answer pairs and gives 
the user a quiz.  

Details:
-- The file format is one line per question and answer pair, question 
   followed by answer, separated by a comma, except that the first line is the 
   names of the things being asked.  For example "state,capital" could the 
   first line, and then other lines would be "California,Sacramento", 
   "Ohio,Columbus", etc.   (See data file given with assignment.)  Note 
   that the questions and answers may have spaces, but not commas.  
-- When the user answers a question, there should be feedback before 
   moving on (say whether the answer was right or wrong, and if it was wrong, 
   say what the right answer is).  
-- This could be done with a "check answer" button and a 
   "next question" button, something like that.  We can discuss layout and 
   flow in class if you want to.
-- You should display the score, how many right from the total.  
   Update it after every answer.
-- So that I can test all of your programs uniformly, let's do 
   this with bundled files.  Put the two data files that I am giving you 
   in a folder called "assets" (at the same level as /lib in your project).  
   You should give the user a choice of which file to be quizzed on. 
-- Format can be multiple choice or fill in the blank.   You can 
   get 5 extra points if you do them both.
